title:: Stochastica
summary:: Raw maps, flows, stochastic processes, distributions, state processes, and explicit sonifiers
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic, UGens>Generators>Chaotic
related:: Classes/HenonMap, Classes/OUProcess, Classes/TGammaRand, Classes/MarkovChain

description::

Stochastica is a SuperCollider suite of chaotic and dynamic UGens. It implements established map equations, dynamical systems, probability algorithms, and stochastic-process models. Whether you are creating complex generative music, simulating unpredictable physical systems, or adding organic variations to sound, this collection provides the mathematical tools to do so natively on the audio server.

A distribution sampler produces independent values when triggered. A stochastic process has memory over time. A discrete map updates a state through a recurrence. A continuous system integrates differential equations. A sonifier maps an internal state to an audible signal and is therefore not the same object as the mathematical system it uses.

Seeded classes use a local PCG32 generator. A nonzero seed is deterministic; zero derives a seed from the parent Synth. Rising triggers and resets use a shared nonpositive-to-positive edge rule.

